    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d57533b2_c1a3313f",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetdEventListenerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 177,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308163
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-12T08:59:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The value is returned by getTransports(), and 0 means nc is null, which also means that the given network is lost or we never get the nc of the given netid.\nAnd passing 0 to NetworkMetrics will make NetworkMetrics.Summary#toString() print nothing to transports.\nSomething like: \n{netId\u003d101, transports\u003d{} ....\n\nYou can refer to https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/frameworks/base/core/java/android/net/metrics/NetworkMetrics.java;l\u003d145?q\u003dnetworkmetrics.java\u0026sq\u003dpackage:%5Eaosp-master$ and https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/libcore/ojluni/src/main/java/java/util/BitSet.java;l\u003d196?q\u003dpackage:%5E(aosp-master)$%20file:(%2F%7C%5E)java%2Futil%2FBitSet%5C.java$\n\nSo that\u0027s why I checked \"transports !\u003d 0\".",
      "parentUuid": "f404400f_8dc60d49",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 177,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 177,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "c49a506a1043d24490732ed5e48771f78ccfb867",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ff8ca5a_f2ba652f",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetdEventListenerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 177,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-12T09:30:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is that it is not a bijection. There is no structural guarantee that a network has any transports, therefore null ⇒ 0 might be reasonable but you can\u0027t assume that 0 ⇒ null.\n\nThis is the only place where getTransports is called. You could have getTransports return a Long, with null if the NC was null, but I think the entire point of this method was to abstract the nullness of the NC from the caller, and now the caller cares about nullness, so the best solution is probably to just inline it. and replace this test with a nullness check.",
      "parentUuid": "d57533b2_c1a3313f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 177,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 177,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "c49a506a1043d24490732ed5e48771f78ccfb867",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
